================================================================================
Rust standard library

Used by:
    every build of hashsync

Like every Rust program, hashsync contains parts of the Rust standard library:
std, core, alloc, compiler_builtins and other crates of the Rust project, and
the crates that they depend on, which are addr2line, adler2, cfg-if, gimli,
hashbrown, libc, memchr, miniz_oxide, object and rustc-demangle.

hashsync uses all of them under the Apache License 2.0, whose text is above,
except for memchr, which it uses under the Unlicense, and compiler_builtins.
compiler_builtins is licensed under the MIT license together with the Apache
License 2.0 with the LLVM exception, and only the MIT license requires a
notice in binaries. Its math functions come from the libm crate, which is
licensed under the MIT license. The MIT license and the copyright notices of
libm follow.

